// name:              The Locksmith - privileged auth-method change triage (one-shot)
// purpose:           For each authentication-method change on a privileged account, answer whether the session that changed the locks belonged to the legitimate user.
// starting_entities: TargetUpn (the account whose methods changed). ChangeTime is optional; without it the last day is scanned.
// required_tables:   AuditLogs, SigninLogs
// optional_tables:   AADNonInteractiveUserSignInLogs (bridge, session walk, footprint), IdentityInfo (assigned roles), OfficeActivity (inbox rules after the change). Each is read through union isfuzzy=true, so a missing table removes its evidence, not the rows.
// variables:         TargetUpn, ChangeTime, PreChangeWindow, PostChangeWindow, IpWindow, BaselineWindow; tuning knobs, AppId, role, ASN and CA lists, weights and thresholds in SECTION 0
// done_criteria:     Every row has a Verdict and Narrative; every Escalate row is escalated; every Review row has each Flag explained (change ticket, out-of-band confirmation with the user, known egress) or is escalated; the ticket records, per change, whether the session that changed the locks was the legitimate user.
// output_type:       analysis
//
// ============================================================================
// THE LOCKSMITH - privileged auth-method change triage, one-shot
// ============================================================================
//
// Someone cut a new key for a privileged door. The Locksmith works out who was
// at the counter, how they proved who they were, where they walked in from and
// what they did once inside, then answers one question per change: was the
// session that changed the locks the legitimate user?
//
// PURPOSE
//   One row per authentication-method change on TargetUpn. Each change is
//   bridged to the initiator's sign-in, that sign-in's session is walked back
//   to its first authentication, the strength of that authentication is
//   tested, the IPs in play are scored against the tenant, privilege is
//   confirmed, the hours after the change are searched for follow-on
//   activity, and a weighted Verdict and a one-sentence Narrative close the
//   row. Single workspace by design: run it in the client workspace that owns
//   the incident.
//
// PARAMETERS (all in SECTION 0)
//   TargetUpn          Required. The privileged account whose methods changed.
//   ChangeTime         Optional UTC datetime. Set: the scan is ChangeTime
//                      +/- ChangeTimeSlack. Null: the scan is the last
//                      DefaultLookback (1d).
//   PreChangeWindow    60m. How far before a change to look for the
//                      initiator's sign-in.
//   PostChangeWindow   4h. How far after a change to look for follow-on
//                      activity, and the add-then-delete span for the
//                      lockout pattern.
//   IpWindow           24h. Footprint: every IP the target and initiators
//                      used in this window, ending at the scan window close.
//   BaselineWindow     30d. Tenant-wide prevalence window for each IP in the
//                      footprint.
//   Everything else    Window plumbing, footprint thresholds, AppId lists,
//                      privileged roles, ASN lists, CA policy IDs, weights and
//                      verdict thresholds. Each is commented where it is set.
//
// READING THE OUTPUT (one row per change, oldest first)
//   Verdict, Score, Narrative, Flags
//       Benign, Review or Escalate; the summed weights; one sentence for the
//       ticket; every flag that fired with its weight.
//   EventTime, OperationName, Action, MethodType, ChangeKind, MethodDetail
//       The change. Action is added, deleted, default changed, updated or
//       added and deleted. ChangeKind is self-service, admin, app or unknown.
//   Target, TargetPrivilege, Initiator, InitiatorPrivilege
//       Who was changed, who changed them, and the roles each holds.
//   ChangeIp*
//       The IP the change came from (audit IP, else bridged sign-in IP) with
//       its FootprintClass, ASN, ASN class, country, baseline users and days.
//       FootprintClass: campaign, novel, egress or VPN, familiar, baseline
//       incomplete (seen only in non-interactive logs, which the baseline
//       skips by default), no sign-in record (audit IP never seen signing in).
//   OtherAccountsOnChangeIp
//       Other accounts that signed in from the change IP within
//       +/- FallbackWindow. Who else was standing in the shop.
//   BridgeMethod, ChangePathClass, Bridge*
//       The sign-in the change was tied to and how. ChangePathClass: expected
//       (My Signins), WHfB provisioning (Windows Sign In), scripted (Graph or
//       PowerShell), unfamiliar app, app-made change, no sign-in bridged.
//   Origin*
//       The first successful authentication of the bridged session:
//       requirement, MFA methods, token-claim seen, risk, device, user agent.
//       OriginPossiblyTruncated means the walk hit SessionLookback, so the
//       real first authentication may be older; token-claim is not trusted
//       there.
//   ChangeDevice*
//       Device on the bridged sign-in: the hands on the keyboard.
//   RegisterCaApplied, RegisterCaPolicies, RegistrationCompletedAt
//       CA policies that look like the "Register security information" user
//       action, and the "registered all required" event that feeds the
//       single-factor-then-registration flag.
//   SessionCountOnDay, SessionIdsOnDay, OriginFlow, BridgeFlow
//       Distinct SessionIds with a successful sign-in for the target on the
//       change day (the session count), and the step-by-step flow of the
//       origin and bridged sign-ins (interrupts, MFA prompts, success),
//       stitched by CorrelationId.
//   PimActivations
//       PIM activations by the target or initiator within +/- PimWindow.
//   AfterHoursActions, InboxRuleActivity, NewMethodInfraIps, LockoutDetail
//       What happened inside PostChangeWindow.
//   UserFootprint
//       Every footprint IP with its class. Identical on every row.
//   EchoesSuppressed
//       App-initiated Update user rows dropped as mirrors of a security-info
//       row on the same target (SECTION 1).
//
// KNOWN LIMITATIONS
//   - No rows means no successful auth-method change on TargetUpn in the scan
//     window. Failed attempts are excluded by design. Check the UPN spelling
//     and ChangeTime before concluding anything.
//   - The bridge is an inference. AuditLogs has no SessionId and its
//     CorrelationId does not reliably match the sign-in tables, so changes are
//     tied to sign-ins by initiator, IP and time. A commented CorrelationId
//     join in SECTION 2 lets you test the direct link in a given tenant.
//   - Graph and PowerShell changes often have no sign-in inside
//     PreChangeWindow because the token is older than the window. The
//     fallback looks for the initiator on the audit IP within
//     +/- FallbackWindow and lists other accounts on that IP. It does not
//     invent a session, and the Narrative says when it was used.
//   - Cookie replay carries the victim's SessionId, so a replayed session
//     walks back to the victim's genuine origin. Token-claim at origin will
//     not fire for that shape; the session ASN hop flag is there for it.
//   - Sign-ins on joined devices using a Primary Refresh Token can carry the
//     same "claim in the token" text at origin. TokenClaimIgnoreRegisteredDevice
//     (default true) suppresses the flag for registered devices.
//   - Both hard flags need a walked session (SessionId present) whose origin
//     is not at the edge of SessionLookback. Without one they cannot fire and
//     the row rests on weights alone.
//   - Single-factor then registration also describes a genuine first-time
//     onboarding on a password, as in a registration campaign. On a privileged
//     account that is still worth an Escalate; close it with the user's
//     confirmation, not the query's.
//   - The IP baseline reads SigninLogs only unless BaselineIncludeNonInteractive
//     is true. IPs seen only in non-interactive logs read "baseline incomplete"
//     rather than "novel".
//   - IdentityInfo AssignedRoles is a snapshot of active roles. A PIM-eligible
//     admin may show no roles until activated, so a PIM activation by the
//     target near the change also counts as privileged.
//   - MethodType is keyword-matched from ResultReason or modifiedProperties.
//     For "default changed" the text may name the old default, not the new.
//   - Follow-on activity is attributed by the target's and initiator's object
//     IDs. Actions taken later by a service principal the attacker created
//     are not followed.
//   - IPv4 versus IPv6 differences between the audit IP and the sign-in IP show
//     up as an IP mismatch or "no sign-in record". Look before you leap.
//
// UNVERIFIED NAMES AND VALUES (confirm against a real incident before trusting)
//   - LoggedByService "Authentication Methods" as supplied; not checked here.
//   - ResultReason naming the method (including Temporary Access Pass
//     issuance), and the verbs in "security info" OperationNames that Action
//     is read from.
//   - StrongAuthentication* property names beyond StrongAuthenticationMethod
//     (PhoneAppDetail, UserDetails, Requirement), and the MethodType integers
//     inside StrongAuthenticationMethod: not mapped, raw values are shown.
//   - PIM activation operation names and where the role name sits in
//     TargetResources.
//   - Follow-on operation names in AppConsentOps, SpCredentialOps and
//     InboxRuleOps (UpdateInboxRules in particular).
//   - AppIds other than My Signins, every ASN number, and the ResultType labels.
//   - SessionId being populated on both sign-in tables.
//   - The authenticationStepResultDetail text "MFA requirement satisfied by
//     claim in the token", and CA result values "success" and "failure".
//
// ============================================================================


// === SECTION 0: The Key Ring ===
// Every analyst input and tuning knob lives here. Nothing investigation-scoped
// appears inline below this block. The derived windows and helpers at the
// bottom are computed, not edited.
//
// --- Investigation inputs ---
let TargetUpn = "";                     // required: the privileged account whose methods were changed
let ChangeTime = datetime(null);        // optional: UTC time of the change; null scans the last DefaultLookback
let PreChangeWindow = 60m;              // look-back from each change for the initiator's sign-in
let PostChangeWindow = 4h;              // look-forward from each change for follow-on activity
let IpWindow = 24h;                     // footprint window, ending at the scan window close
let BaselineWindow = 30d;               // tenant-wide prevalence window for every footprint IP
//
// --- Window plumbing ---
let DefaultLookback = 1d;               // scan width when ChangeTime is null
let ChangeTimeSlack = 15m;              // scan half-width either side of ChangeTime when it is set
let BridgeSkew = 2m;                    // audit and sign-in clocks disagree; a bridged sign-in may land this far after the change
let FallbackWindow = 10m;               // +/- window for the IP fallback bridge and the other-accounts check
let SessionLookback = 7d;               // how far back the session walk may go for its first authentication
let OriginBoundaryTolerance = 1h;       // an origin this close to the start of the walk may be older than we can see
let EchoWindow = 2m;                    // app-initiated Update user rows this close to a security-info row are echoes
let PimWindow = 4h;                     // +/- window for PIM activations around each change
let IdentityInfoLookback = 14d;         // how far back to look for the latest IdentityInfo record
let NoveltyWindow = 1d;                 // "first seen today": first seen within this before the scan window opened
//
// --- Footprint classification ---
let BaselineIncludeNonInteractive = false;  // true adds the non-interactive table to the IP baseline; costly in big tenants
let EgressMinUsers = 5;                 // at least this many users ...
let EgressMinDays = 7;                  // ... over at least this many days reads as egress or VPN
let CampaignMinUsers = 3;               // at least this many users on an IP first seen inside NoveltyWindow reads as campaign
//
// --- Change path apps, matched on AppId, never on display name ---
let MySigninsAppId = "19db86c3-b2b9-44cc-b339-36da233a3be2";    // My Signins: the expected path
//
// AppIds this client treats as expected. Keep the placeholder so the list is
// never empty; add real entries alongside it.
let AdditionalExpectedAppIds = dynamic(["__locksmith_placeholder__"]);
//
// Windows Sign In, which suggests WHfB provisioning. AppId from memory, not
// verified against a live tenant.
let WindowsSignInAppIds = dynamic(["38aa3b87-a06d-4817-b275-7a316988d93b"]);
//
// Scripting and API clients. First-party AppIds from memory; confirm them in
// the client's sign-in logs. Display-name matching on "PowerShell" and
// "Command Line" in SECTION 8 is a backstop for clients missing here.
let ScriptedAppIds = dynamic([
    "14d82eec-204b-4c2f-b7e8-296a70dab67e",   // Microsoft Graph Command Line Tools
    "de8bc8b5-d9f9-48b1-a8ad-b748da725064",   // Graph Explorer
    "1b730954-1685-4b74-9bfd-dac224a7b894",   // Azure Active Directory PowerShell
    "1950a258-227b-4e31-a9cf-717495945fc2",   // Microsoft Azure PowerShell
    "04b07795-8ddb-461a-bbee-02f9e1bf7b46"    // Microsoft Azure CLI
]);
//
// --- Privileged roles, matched against IdentityInfo AssignedRoles ---
// Same list as deep-dive.kql so the family agrees on what privileged means.
let PrivilegedRoles = dynamic([
    "Global Administrator", "Privileged Role Administrator",
    "Privileged Authentication Administrator", "Security Administrator",
    "Exchange Administrator", "SharePoint Administrator",
    "User Administrator", "Application Administrator",
    "Cloud Application Administrator", "Intune Administrator",
    "Conditional Access Administrator", "Helpdesk Administrator",
    "Password Administrator", "Authentication Administrator",
    "Directory Synchronization Accounts"
]);
//
// --- ASN lists, compared as strings against AutonomousSystemNumber ---
// Hosting and VPS providers. Starter list, numbers from memory: verify and
// extend per client. Cloudflare (13335) is left out on purpose: WARP and
// iCloud Private Relay make it ordinary consumer egress.
let HostingAsns = dynamic([
    "16509", "14618",       // Amazon
    "15169", "396982",      // Google, Google Cloud
    "14061",                // DigitalOcean
    "16276",                // OVH
    "24940",                // Hetzner
    "63949",                // Akamai Connected Cloud (Linode)
    "20473",                // Vultr (Choopa)
    "9009",                 // M247
    "60068", "212238",      // Datacamp (CDN77)
    "45102",                // Alibaba Cloud
    "31898",                // Oracle Cloud
    "51167",                // Contabo
    "36352",                // ColoCrossing
    "53667"                 // FranTech (BuyVM)
]);
//
// Microsoft. Kept apart from hosting with a lower weight: Azure Virtual
// Desktop, Windows 365 and Microsoft-hosted egress are routine for some
// clients, but Azure is also a popular AiTM host. Numbers from memory; verify.
let MicrosoftAsns = dynamic(["8075", "8068", "8069", "12076"]);
//
// --- Conditional Access: the "Register security information" user action ---
// Sign-in logs record which policies applied, not which user action a policy
// targets. Put this client's policy object IDs here for an exact match. The
// name regex is a heuristic fallback and is labelled as one in the output.
let RegisterSecInfoPolicyIds = dynamic(["__locksmith_placeholder__"]);
let RegisterSecInfoUseNameHeuristic = true;
let RegisterSecInfoNameRegex = @"(?i)(security info|registration|register)";
//
// --- Follow-on operations for SECTION 7. Names from memory; verify. ---
let AppConsentOps = dynamic(["Consent to application", "Add delegated permission grant", "Add app role assignment to service principal"]);
let SpCredentialOps = dynamic(["Add service principal credentials"]);
// Application secret and certificate changes log as "Update application",
// a dash, then "Certificates and secrets management". SECTION 7 matches the
// trailing phrase so the dash character never has to be typed.
let InboxRuleOps = dynamic(["New-InboxRule", "Set-InboxRule", "UpdateInboxRules"]);
//
// --- Verdict weights and thresholds ---
let W_TokenClaimAtOrigin    = 40;   // hard flag: MFA satisfied by a claim at the session's first authentication
let W_SingleFactorThenReg   = 40;   // hard flag: single-factor origin, then "registered all required security info"
let W_CampaignIp            = 35;
let W_LockoutPattern        = 30;
let W_PrivilegedActionAfter = 30;
let W_NovelIp               = 25;
let W_HostingAsn            = 25;
let W_PhoneDowngrade        = 25;
let W_ScriptedChangePath    = 25;
let W_UnfamiliarChangePath  = 20;
let W_NewMethodFromNewInfra = 20;
let W_InboxRuleAfter        = 20;
let W_RiskySignin           = 20;
let W_SessionAsnHop         = 15;
let W_TapIssued             = 15;
let W_AppMadeChange         = 15;
let W_MicrosoftAsn          = 10;
let W_UnmanagedDevice       = 10;
let W_NoSigninBridged       = 10;
let W_ChangeIpUnseen        = 10;
let W_FallbackBridge        = 5;
let W_BaselineIncomplete    = 5;
let W_NoRegisterCaPolicy    = 5;
let ReviewThreshold         = 20;
let EscalateThreshold       = 50;
let HardFlagsForceEscalate  = true;     // only the two hard flags above force Escalate; everything else is weight
let TokenClaimIgnoreRegisteredDevice = true;   // PRT sign-ins on registered devices carry the same claim text
//
// --- Derived windows (computed, do not edit) ---
let AnchorSet = isnotnull(ChangeTime);
let ScanStart = iff(AnchorSet, ChangeTime - ChangeTimeSlack, now() - DefaultLookback);
let ScanEnd = iff(AnchorSet, ChangeTime + ChangeTimeSlack, now());
let AuditStart = ScanStart - max_of(PimWindow, PostChangeWindow, PreChangeWindow);
let AuditEnd = ScanEnd + max_of(PimWindow, PostChangeWindow);
let FootprintStart = min_of(ScanEnd - IpWindow, ScanStart - PreChangeWindow);
let FootprintEnd = ScanEnd + PostChangeWindow;
let UserPullStart = min_of(startofday(ScanStart), FootprintStart, ScanStart - FallbackWindow);
let UserPullEnd = max_of(startofday(ScanEnd) + 1d, FootprintEnd);
let SessionWalkStart = ScanStart - SessionLookback;
let BaselineStart = ScanEnd - BaselineWindow;
let NoveltyStart = ScanStart - NoveltyWindow;
let TargetUpnLc = tolower(TargetUpn);
let EmptySetGuard = dynamic(["__locksmith_none__"]);
let TokenClaimText = "MFA requirement satisfied by claim in the token";
let FallbackMinutes = tostring(toint(FallbackWindow / 1m));
//
// --- Helpers ---
// Some modifiedProperties values arrive as JSON inside a string inside JSON.
let ParseNested = (v:dynamic) {
    let p = parse_json(tostring(v));
    iff(gettype(p) == "string", parse_json(tostring(p)), p)
};
//
// Method family from free text. Order matters: "Phone app notification" is
// the Authenticator, not a phone. Wording in ResultReason is not verified, so
// anything unmatched comes back "Unknown" rather than guessed.
let MethodFromText = (t:string) {
    case(
        t contains "temporary access pass" or t contains "TemporaryAccessPass", "Temporary Access Pass",
        t contains "FIDO" or t contains "passkey" or t contains "security key", "FIDO2 or passkey",
        t contains "Windows Hello" or t contains "WindowsHello", "Windows Hello for Business",
        t contains "Authenticator" or t contains "PhoneApp" or t contains "app notification" or t contains "mobile app", "Microsoft Authenticator",
        t contains "SMS" or t contains "text message", "Phone (SMS)",
        t contains "voice" or t contains "phone call" or t contains "office phone", "Phone (voice)",
        t contains "phone", "Phone (unspecified)",
        t contains "OATH" or t contains "hardware token" or t contains "software token", "OATH token",
        t contains "email", "Email",
        t contains "password", "Password",
        "Unknown")
};
//
// A sign-in method counts as "the new method" when the families agree.
// Authenticator codes show up in sign-ins as OATH verification codes.
let MethodsMatch = (changed:string, used:string) {
    changed == used
    or (changed startswith "Phone" and used startswith "Phone"
        and (changed == "Phone (unspecified)" or used == "Phone (unspecified)"))
    or (changed == "Microsoft Authenticator" and used == "OATH token")
};
//
// Labels for the flow steps in SECTION 5. From memory; blank when unknown.
let ResultLabel = (r:string) {
    case(
        r == "0", "success",
        r == "50074", "MFA required",
        r == "50076", "MFA required by policy",
        r == "50072", "MFA registration required",
        r == "50079", "MFA registration required",
        r == "50125", "password reset or registration interrupt",
        r == "50140", "keep-me-signed-in interrupt",
        r == "50158", "external security challenge",
        r == "50126", "bad credentials",
        r == "53003", "blocked by Conditional Access",
        "")
};
// === SECTION 1: The Keys Cut ===
// Every key cut for this door. One AuditLogs read, pre-filtered to the shapes
// any later section needs (method changes, PIM, follow-on operations), then
// split. Two change shapes:
//   a) LoggedByService "Authentication Methods" and OperationName has
//      "security info". No operation list is hard-coded; Action is read from
//      the verb in the operation name.
//   b) "Update user" whose modifiedProperties touch StrongAuthentication*.
//      contains, not has: "StrongAuthenticationMethod" is one term.
let AuditContext = materialize(
    AuditLogs
    | where TimeGenerated between (AuditStart .. AuditEnd)
    | where (LoggedByService == "Authentication Methods" and OperationName has "security info")
        or (OperationName == "Update user" and tostring(TargetResources) contains "StrongAuthentication")
        or (LoggedByService == "PIM" and OperationName has "PIM activation")
        or OperationName has "member to role"
        or OperationName in~ (AppConsentOps)
        or OperationName in~ (SpCredentialOps)
        or OperationName has "Certificates and secrets management"
        or OperationName has "conditional access policy"
    | project TimeGenerated, Id, OperationName, LoggedByService, Result, ResultReason,
        InitiatedBy, TargetResources, CorrelationId
);
//
// Successful changes on the target only. TargetResources[0] matches the rest
// of this family; if a client's logs put the user in another slot, this is
// where rows go missing.
let MethodEventsRaw =
    AuditContext
    | where (LoggedByService == "Authentication Methods" and OperationName has "security info")
        or (OperationName == "Update user" and tostring(TargetResources) contains "StrongAuthentication")
    | where Result =~ "success"
    | extend
        TargetUpnLower = tolower(tostring(TargetResources[0].userPrincipalName)),
        TargetId = tostring(TargetResources[0].id),
        InitiatorUpn = tolower(tostring(InitiatedBy.user.userPrincipalName)),
        InitiatorId = tostring(InitiatedBy.user.id),
        InitiatorIp = tostring(InitiatedBy.user.ipAddress),
        InitiatorAppName = tostring(InitiatedBy.app.displayName),
        InitiatorAppId = tostring(InitiatedBy.app.appId)
    | where isnotempty(TargetUpnLc) and TargetUpnLower == TargetUpnLc;
//
// Shape a. "registered all required" and the started / reviewed / canceled
// events are context, not changes: they never become scored rows, but
// "registration completed" feeds the SECTION 3 hard flag.
let SecInfoRows =
    MethodEventsRaw
    | where OperationName != "Update user"
    | extend Action = case(
        OperationName has "all required", "registration completed",
        OperationName has_any ("started", "reviewed", "canceled", "cancelled"), "informational",
        OperationName has "default", "default changed",
        OperationName has "deleted", "deleted",
        OperationName has "registered", "added",
        OperationName has_any ("updated", "changed"), "updated",
        "other")
    | extend MethodType = MethodFromText(ResultReason)
    | extend MethodType = iff(MethodType == "Unknown",
        MethodFromText(tostring(TargetResources[0].modifiedProperties)), MethodType)
    | extend
        MethodDetail = ResultReason,
        ModifiedProps = substring(tostring(TargetResources[0].modifiedProperties), 0, 500);
//
// Shape b. Action comes from comparing old and new values per property:
// more entries is added, fewer is deleted, same count with a different
// Default entry in StrongAuthenticationMethod is default changed. The
// MethodType integers are not mapped (unverified); raw values are kept.
let StrongAuthRows =
    MethodEventsRaw
    | where OperationName == "Update user"
    | mv-apply mp = TargetResources[0].modifiedProperties on (
        where tostring(mp.displayName) startswith "StrongAuthentication"
        | extend
            PropName = tostring(mp.displayName),
            OldText = tostring(ParseNested(mp.oldValue)),
            NewText = tostring(ParseNested(mp.newValue))
        | extend
            OldCount = coalesce(array_length(parse_json(OldText)), 0),
            NewCount = coalesce(array_length(parse_json(NewText)), 0),
            OldDefault = extract(@'"MethodType"\s*:\s*(\d+)', 1,
                extract(@'\{[^{}]*"Default"\s*:\s*true[^{}]*\}', 0, OldText)),
            NewDefault = extract(@'"MethodType"\s*:\s*(\d+)', 1,
                extract(@'\{[^{}]*"Default"\s*:\s*true[^{}]*\}', 0, NewText))
        | extend PropAction = case(
            NewCount > OldCount, "added",
            NewCount < OldCount, "deleted",
            PropName == "StrongAuthenticationMethod" and OldDefault != NewDefault, "default changed",
            "updated")
        | summarize
            SaProps = make_set(PropName),
            SaActions = make_set(PropAction),
            SaDetail = strcat_array(make_list(strcat(PropName, ": ",
                substring(OldText, 0, 200), " -> ", substring(NewText, 0, 200)), 8), " | ")
    )
    | where array_length(SaProps) > 0
    | extend Action = case(
        set_has_element(SaActions, "added") and set_has_element(SaActions, "deleted"), "added and deleted",
        set_has_element(SaActions, "deleted"), "deleted",
        set_has_element(SaActions, "added"), "added",
        set_has_element(SaActions, "default changed"), "default changed",
        "updated")
    | extend MethodType = iff(
        array_length(SaProps) == 1 and set_has_element(SaProps, "StrongAuthenticationRequirement"),
        "Per-user MFA requirement", MethodFromText(SaDetail))
    | extend
        MethodDetail = "Update user (StrongAuthentication properties)",
        ModifiedProps = SaDetail
    | project-away SaProps, SaActions, SaDetail;
//
let MethodEvents = materialize(
    union SecInfoRows, StrongAuthRows
    | extend TargetKey = TargetUpnLower
    | extend ChangeKind = case(
        isnotempty(InitiatorId) and InitiatorId == TargetId, "self-service",
        isnotempty(InitiatorUpn) and InitiatorUpn == TargetUpnLower, "self-service",
        isnotempty(InitiatorId) or isnotempty(InitiatorUpn), "admin",
        isnotempty(InitiatorAppId) or isnotempty(InitiatorAppName), "app",
        "unknown")
    | extend IsScored = Action !in ("registration completed", "informational")
);
//
// Echo suppression. A user's own registration is often mirrored seconds
// later by an app-initiated "Update user" StrongAuthentication* row. Counting
// it would double the change and trip the app flag. An echo must sit on the
// same target user as the security-info row it mirrors: the join is on
// TargetKey, not just on time.
let EchoIds = materialize(
    MethodEvents
    | where OperationName == "Update user" and ChangeKind == "app"
    | project EchoId = Id, EchoTime = TimeGenerated, EchoTargetKey = TargetKey
    | join kind=inner (
        MethodEvents
        | where OperationName != "Update user" and IsScored
        | project SecTime = TimeGenerated, SecTargetKey = TargetKey
    ) on $left.EchoTargetKey == $right.SecTargetKey
    | where EchoTime between ((SecTime - EchoWindow) .. (SecTime + EchoWindow))
    | distinct EchoId
);
let EchoCount = toscalar(EchoIds | count);
//
// Every real change across the audit pull (used for the lockout pairing), and
// the ones inside the scan window, which become the output rows.
let MethodChanges = materialize(
    MethodEvents
    | where IsScored
    | where Id !in (EchoIds)
);
let Changes = materialize(
    MethodChanges
    | where TimeGenerated between (ScanStart .. ScanEnd)
    | extend
        IsTapIssued = MethodType == "Temporary Access Pass" and Action == "added",
        IsAppMadeChange = ChangeKind == "app"
    | project ChangeId = Id, EventTime = TimeGenerated, OperationName, Action, MethodType,
        MethodDetail, ModifiedProps, ChangeKind, TargetUpnLower, TargetId, TargetKey,
        InitiatorUpn, InitiatorId, InitiatorIp, InitiatorAppName, InitiatorAppId,
        IsTapIssued, IsAppMadeChange, AuditCorrelationId = CorrelationId
);
let RegistrationsCompleted =
    MethodEvents
    | where Action == "registration completed"
    | project RegTime = TimeGenerated, RegTargetKey = TargetKey;
// === SECTION 2: The Customer ===
// Who was at the counter. Each change is tied to the INITIATOR's closest
// successful sign-in before it (not the target's), within PreChangeWindow,
// preferring one from the audit IP. Both sign-in tables are read, scoped to
// the users in play and the windows here; the non-interactive table is big.
// The non-interactive columns DeviceDetail, LocationDetails,
// AuthenticationDetails and ConditionalAccessPolicies are strings, so every
// leg goes through parse_json(tostring()).
let InitiatorIdSet = array_concat(
    toscalar(Changes | where isnotempty(InitiatorId) | summarize make_set(InitiatorId)), EmptySetGuard);
let TargetIdSet = array_concat(
    toscalar(MethodEvents | where isnotempty(TargetId) | summarize make_set(TargetId)), EmptySetGuard);
let UserIdSet = set_union(InitiatorIdSet, TargetIdSet);
let UpnSet = array_concat(
    toscalar(Changes | where isnotempty(InitiatorUpn) | summarize make_set(InitiatorUpn)), pack_array(TargetUpnLc));
let InitiatorIpSet = array_concat(
    toscalar(Changes | where isnotempty(InitiatorIp) | summarize make_set(InitiatorIp)), EmptySetGuard);
//
// Target and initiators, one pull covering the bridge, footprint, session
// count and post-change windows.
let UserSignins = materialize(
    union isfuzzy=true
        (SigninLogs
        | where TimeGenerated between (UserPullStart .. UserPullEnd)
        | where UserId in (UserIdSet) or (isnotempty(TargetUpnLc) and UserPrincipalName =~ TargetUpnLc)
        | project TimeGenerated, SigninTable = "interactive", UserId, UserPrincipalName = tolower(UserPrincipalName),
            IPAddress, AppId, AppDisplayName, ResultType = tostring(ResultType), SessionId, CorrelationId,
            Asn = iff(tostring(AutonomousSystemNumber) in ("", "0"), "", tostring(AutonomousSystemNumber)),
            Country = tostring(parse_json(tostring(LocationDetails)).countryOrRegion),
            AuthenticationRequirement, AuthDetailsRaw = tostring(AuthenticationDetails),
            CaRaw = tostring(ConditionalAccessPolicies), DeviceRaw = tostring(DeviceDetail),
            RiskLevelDuringSignIn, UserAgent),
        (AADNonInteractiveUserSignInLogs
        | where TimeGenerated between (UserPullStart .. UserPullEnd)
        | where UserId in (UserIdSet) or (isnotempty(TargetUpnLc) and UserPrincipalName =~ TargetUpnLc)
        | project TimeGenerated, SigninTable = "non-interactive", UserId, UserPrincipalName = tolower(UserPrincipalName),
            IPAddress, AppId, AppDisplayName, ResultType = tostring(ResultType), SessionId, CorrelationId,
            Asn = iff(tostring(AutonomousSystemNumber) in ("", "0"), "", tostring(AutonomousSystemNumber)),
            Country = tostring(parse_json(tostring(LocationDetails)).countryOrRegion),
            AuthenticationRequirement, AuthDetailsRaw = tostring(AuthenticationDetails),
            CaRaw = tostring(ConditionalAccessPolicies), DeviceRaw = tostring(DeviceDetail),
            RiskLevelDuringSignIn, UserAgent)
);
//
// Anyone signing in from an audit IP around the scan window. Feeds the
// fallback bridge and the other-accounts check.
let IpFallbackSignins = materialize(
    union isfuzzy=true
        (SigninLogs
        | where TimeGenerated between ((ScanStart - FallbackWindow) .. (ScanEnd + FallbackWindow))
        | where IPAddress in (InitiatorIpSet)
        | where tostring(ResultType) == "0"
        | project TimeGenerated, SigninTable = "interactive", UserId, UserPrincipalName = tolower(UserPrincipalName),
            IPAddress, AppId, AppDisplayName, SessionId, CorrelationId,
            Asn = iff(tostring(AutonomousSystemNumber) in ("", "0"), "", tostring(AutonomousSystemNumber)),
            Country = tostring(parse_json(tostring(LocationDetails)).countryOrRegion),
            AuthenticationRequirement, AuthDetailsRaw = tostring(AuthenticationDetails),
            DeviceRaw = tostring(DeviceDetail), RiskLevelDuringSignIn, UserAgent),
        (AADNonInteractiveUserSignInLogs
        | where TimeGenerated between ((ScanStart - FallbackWindow) .. (ScanEnd + FallbackWindow))
        | where IPAddress in (InitiatorIpSet)
        | where tostring(ResultType) == "0"
        | project TimeGenerated, SigninTable = "non-interactive", UserId, UserPrincipalName = tolower(UserPrincipalName),
            IPAddress, AppId, AppDisplayName, SessionId, CorrelationId,
            Asn = iff(tostring(AutonomousSystemNumber) in ("", "0"), "", tostring(AutonomousSystemNumber)),
            Country = tostring(parse_json(tostring(LocationDetails)).countryOrRegion),
            AuthenticationRequirement, AuthDetailsRaw = tostring(AuthenticationDetails),
            DeviceRaw = tostring(DeviceDetail), RiskLevelDuringSignIn, UserAgent)
);
//
// Primary bridge: initiator, successful, [change - PreChangeWindow, change +
// BridgeSkew]. Rank: audit IP match first, then nearest in time, then
// interactive over non-interactive.
let BridgePrimary = materialize(
    Changes
    | where isnotempty(InitiatorId)
    | project ChangeId, EventTime, InitiatorId, InitiatorIp
    | join kind=inner (
        UserSignins
        | where ResultType == "0"
        | project BridgeTime = TimeGenerated, BridgeTable = SigninTable, BridgeUserId = UserId,
            BridgeUpn = UserPrincipalName, BridgeIp = IPAddress, BridgeAppId = AppId,
            BridgeAppName = AppDisplayName, BridgeSessionId = SessionId,
            BridgeCorrelationId = CorrelationId, BridgeAsn = Asn, BridgeCountry = Country,
            BridgeAuthReq = AuthenticationRequirement, BridgeAuthDetailsRaw = AuthDetailsRaw,
            BridgeDeviceRaw = DeviceRaw, BridgeRisk = RiskLevelDuringSignIn, BridgeUserAgent = UserAgent
    ) on $left.InitiatorId == $right.BridgeUserId
    | where BridgeTime between ((EventTime - PreChangeWindow) .. (EventTime + BridgeSkew))
    | extend BridgeIpMatch = isnotempty(InitiatorIp) and BridgeIp == InitiatorIp
    | extend BridgeRank = iff(BridgeIpMatch, 0, 100000000)
        + abs(datetime_diff("second", EventTime, BridgeTime)) * 2
        + iff(BridgeTable == "interactive", 0, 1)
    | summarize arg_min(BridgeRank, *) by ChangeId
    | extend BridgeMethod = case(
        BridgeIpMatch, "initiator + IP + time",
        isempty(InitiatorIp), "initiator + time (no audit IP)",
        "initiator + time (audit IP did not match)")
    | project-away EventTime, InitiatorId, InitiatorIp, BridgeRank
);
//
// Fallback bridge, typical of Graph and PowerShell changes whose token is
// older than PreChangeWindow: the initiator on the audit IP within
// +/- FallbackWindow. Sign-ins by other accounts on that IP are never used as
// the bridge; they are reported in SECTION 8 as OtherAccountsOnChangeIp.
let BridgeFallback =
    Changes
    | where isnotempty(InitiatorId) and isnotempty(InitiatorIp)
    | project ChangeId, EventTime, InitiatorId, InitiatorIp
    | join kind=leftanti BridgePrimary on ChangeId
    | join kind=inner (
        IpFallbackSignins
        | project BridgeTime = TimeGenerated, BridgeTable = SigninTable, BridgeUserId = UserId,
            BridgeUpn = UserPrincipalName, BridgeIp = IPAddress, BridgeAppId = AppId,
            BridgeAppName = AppDisplayName, BridgeSessionId = SessionId,
            BridgeCorrelationId = CorrelationId, BridgeAsn = Asn, BridgeCountry = Country,
            BridgeAuthReq = AuthenticationRequirement, BridgeAuthDetailsRaw = AuthDetailsRaw,
            BridgeDeviceRaw = DeviceRaw, BridgeRisk = RiskLevelDuringSignIn, BridgeUserAgent = UserAgent
    ) on $left.InitiatorIp == $right.BridgeIp
    | where BridgeUserId == InitiatorId
    | where BridgeTime between ((EventTime - FallbackWindow) .. (EventTime + FallbackWindow))
    | extend BridgeIpMatch = true, BridgeRank = abs(datetime_diff("second", EventTime, BridgeTime))
    | summarize arg_min(BridgeRank, *) by ChangeId
    | extend BridgeMethod = "fallback: initiator on the audit IP within FallbackWindow"
    | project-away EventTime, InitiatorId, InitiatorIp, BridgeRank;
let Bridge = materialize(union BridgePrimary, BridgeFallback);
//
// --- Commented-out CorrelationId bridge, for testing only ---
// AuditLogs.CorrelationId does not reliably equal the sign-in CorrelationId.
// To test it in a tenant: set TargetUpn and ChangeTime to a known-good
// self-service registration, uncomment this block and the CORRELATION TEST
// line at the very end of the query, and check whether CorrSigninTime lands
// seconds before EventTime on the expected AppId. If it does across several
// known-good cases, it is a usable tie-breaker in that tenant.
//
// let CorrelationBridge =
//     Changes
//     | project ChangeId, AuditCorrelationId
//     | join kind=inner (
//         UserSignins
//         | project CorrelationId, CorrSigninTime = TimeGenerated, CorrAppId = AppId,
//             CorrSessionId = SessionId, CorrIp = IPAddress
//     ) on $left.AuditCorrelationId == $right.CorrelationId
//     | summarize arg_max(CorrSigninTime, CorrAppId, CorrSessionId, CorrIp) by ChangeId;
//
// Session walk: every record carrying a bridged SessionId, back to
// SessionLookback, scoped by user and SessionId.
let BridgedSessionIds = array_concat(
    toscalar(Bridge | where isnotempty(BridgeSessionId) | summarize make_set(BridgeSessionId)), EmptySetGuard);
let BridgedUserIds = array_concat(
    toscalar(Bridge | summarize make_set(BridgeUserId)), EmptySetGuard);
let SessionRows =
    union isfuzzy=true
        (SigninLogs
        | where TimeGenerated between (SessionWalkStart .. FootprintEnd)
        | where UserId in (BridgedUserIds)
        | where SessionId in (BridgedSessionIds)
        | project TimeGenerated, SigninTable = "interactive", SessionId, ResultType = tostring(ResultType),
            IPAddress, AppDisplayName, CorrelationId,
            Asn = iff(tostring(AutonomousSystemNumber) in ("", "0"), "", tostring(AutonomousSystemNumber)),
            Country = tostring(parse_json(tostring(LocationDetails)).countryOrRegion),
            AuthenticationRequirement, AuthDetailsRaw = tostring(AuthenticationDetails),
            DeviceRaw = tostring(DeviceDetail), RiskLevelDuringSignIn, UserAgent),
        (AADNonInteractiveUserSignInLogs
        | where TimeGenerated between (SessionWalkStart .. FootprintEnd)
        | where UserId in (BridgedUserIds)
        | where SessionId in (BridgedSessionIds)
        | project TimeGenerated, SigninTable = "non-interactive", SessionId, ResultType = tostring(ResultType),
            IPAddress, AppDisplayName, CorrelationId,
            Asn = iff(tostring(AutonomousSystemNumber) in ("", "0"), "", tostring(AutonomousSystemNumber)),
            Country = tostring(parse_json(tostring(LocationDetails)).countryOrRegion),
            AuthenticationRequirement, AuthDetailsRaw = tostring(AuthenticationDetails),
            DeviceRaw = tostring(DeviceDetail), RiskLevelDuringSignIn, UserAgent);
//
// First successful authentication per session.
let SessionOrigins = materialize(
    SessionRows
    | where ResultType == "0"
    | summarize arg_min(TimeGenerated, SigninTable, IPAddress, AppDisplayName, Asn, Country,
        AuthenticationRequirement, AuthDetailsRaw, DeviceRaw, RiskLevelDuringSignIn, UserAgent,
        CorrelationId) by SessionId
    | project WalkSessionId = SessionId, WalkOriginTime = TimeGenerated, WalkOriginTable = SigninTable,
        WalkOriginIp = IPAddress, WalkOriginAppName = AppDisplayName, WalkOriginAsn = Asn,
        WalkOriginCountry = Country, WalkOriginAuthReq = AuthenticationRequirement,
        WalkOriginAuthDetailsRaw = AuthDetailsRaw, WalkOriginDeviceRaw = DeviceRaw,
        WalkOriginRisk = RiskLevelDuringSignIn, WalkOriginUserAgent = UserAgent,
        WalkOriginCorrelationId = CorrelationId
);
// === SECTION 3: The Strength Test ===
// How the customer proved who they were, read from the session's first
// authentication. Where no session could be walked, the bridged sign-in
// stands in and OriginSource says so.
//
// Hard flags. Both need a walked session whose origin is not at the edge of
// the walk (OriginPossiblyTruncated): a bridged sign-in with no session may be
// mid-session, where a token claim is normal.
//   - Token-claim MFA at origin: the first record of the session reads "MFA
//     requirement satisfied by claim in the token" and shows no MFA method of
//     its own. Suppressed for registered devices while
//     TokenClaimIgnoreRegisteredDevice is true (PRT sign-ins look the same).
//   - Single-factor then registration: an interactive origin with
//     AuthenticationRequirement singleFactorAuthentication, no MFA method and
//     no token claim in AuthenticationDetails, then "User registered all
//     required security info" for the same target. AuthenticationRequirement
//     alone records what was required, not what was done, and
//     non-interactive refreshes routinely read single-factor, hence the extra
//     conditions. Someone enrolling their own MFA on a password alone.
let Spine = materialize(
    Changes
    | lookup kind=leftouter Bridge on ChangeId
    | lookup kind=leftouter SessionOrigins on $left.BridgeSessionId == $right.WalkSessionId
    | extend OriginSource = case(
        isnotnull(WalkOriginTime), "session walk",
        isnotnull(BridgeTime), "bridged sign-in (no session walk)",
        "none")
    | extend UseWalk = OriginSource == "session walk"
    | extend
        OriginTime = iff(UseWalk, WalkOriginTime, BridgeTime),
        OriginTable = iff(UseWalk, WalkOriginTable, BridgeTable),
        OriginIp = iff(UseWalk, WalkOriginIp, BridgeIp),
        OriginAppName = iff(UseWalk, WalkOriginAppName, BridgeAppName),
        OriginAsn = iff(UseWalk, WalkOriginAsn, BridgeAsn),
        OriginCountry = iff(UseWalk, WalkOriginCountry, BridgeCountry),
        OriginAuthRequirement = iff(UseWalk, WalkOriginAuthReq, BridgeAuthReq),
        OriginAuthDetailsRaw = iff(UseWalk, WalkOriginAuthDetailsRaw, BridgeAuthDetailsRaw),
        OriginDeviceRaw = iff(UseWalk, WalkOriginDeviceRaw, BridgeDeviceRaw),
        OriginRisk = iff(UseWalk, WalkOriginRisk, BridgeRisk),
        OriginUserAgent = iff(UseWalk, WalkOriginUserAgent, BridgeUserAgent),
        OriginCorrelationId = iff(UseWalk, WalkOriginCorrelationId, BridgeCorrelationId)
);
//
// Methods that succeeded at origin, parsed from AuthenticationDetails.
let OriginMethods =
    Spine
    | where isnotempty(OriginAuthDetailsRaw)
    | project ChangeId, ad = parse_json(OriginAuthDetailsRaw)
    | mv-expand ad
    | where tobool(ad.succeeded)
    | summarize OriginMethodsUsed = make_set(tostring(ad.authenticationMethod)) by ChangeId;
//
// "Registered all required security info" for the same target, after the
// origin and around the change. Feeds the single-factor hard flag.
let RegAfterChange =
    Spine
    | project ChangeId, TargetKey, EventTime, OriginTime
    | join kind=inner RegistrationsCompleted on $left.TargetKey == $right.RegTargetKey
    | where RegTime between ((EventTime - PreChangeWindow) .. (EventTime + PostChangeWindow))
    | where isnull(OriginTime) or RegTime >= OriginTime
    | summarize RegistrationCompletedAt = min(RegTime) by ChangeId;
//
// CA policies on the initiator's sign-ins in the pre-change window that match
// the "Register security information" policy IDs, or by name if the
// heuristic is on. Only applied results count (success or failure).
let RegisterCaByChange =
    Changes
    | project ChangeId, EventTime, InitiatorId
    | join kind=inner (
        UserSignins
        | where TimeGenerated between ((ScanStart - PreChangeWindow) .. (ScanEnd + BridgeSkew))
        | where UserId in (InitiatorIdSet)
        | where CaRaw has "displayName"
        | mv-expand cap = parse_json(CaRaw)
        | extend CapId = tostring(cap.id), CapName = tostring(cap.displayName), CapResult = tostring(cap.result)
        | where CapResult in ("success", "failure")
        | extend CapMatchedBy = case(
            CapId in (RegisterSecInfoPolicyIds), "policy id",
            RegisterSecInfoUseNameHeuristic and CapName matches regex RegisterSecInfoNameRegex, "name heuristic",
            "")
        | where isnotempty(CapMatchedBy)
        | project CaTime = TimeGenerated, CaUserId = UserId,
            CaPolicy = strcat(CapName, " (", CapResult, ", ", CapMatchedBy, ")")
    ) on $left.InitiatorId == $right.CaUserId
    | where CaTime between ((EventTime - PreChangeWindow) .. (EventTime + BridgeSkew))
    | summarize RegisterCaPolicies = make_set(CaPolicy, 10) by ChangeId;
// === SECTION 4: The Footprint ===
// Where they walked in from. Every IP the target and initiators used in
// IpWindow (both sign-in tables), plus any audit IP that never signed in,
// scored against the tenant over BaselineWindow.
let FootprintSigninIps = materialize(
    UserSignins
    | where TimeGenerated between (FootprintStart .. FootprintEnd)
    | where isnotempty(IPAddress)
    | summarize
        InteractiveHits = countif(SigninTable == "interactive"),
        NonInteractiveHits = countif(SigninTable == "non-interactive"),
        FootprintAsn = take_anyif(Asn, isnotempty(Asn)),
        FootprintCountry = take_anyif(Country, isnotempty(Country)),
        TargetFirstInFootprint = minif(TimeGenerated, UserId in (TargetIdSet) or UserPrincipalName == TargetUpnLc)
        by IPAddress
);
let FootprintIps =
    union
        FootprintSigninIps,
        (Changes
        | where isnotempty(InitiatorIp)
        | distinct IPAddress = InitiatorIp
        | join kind=leftanti FootprintSigninIps on IPAddress
        | extend InteractiveHits = tolong(0), NonInteractiveHits = tolong(0));
let FootprintIpSet = array_concat(
    toscalar(FootprintIps | summarize make_set(IPAddress)), EmptySetGuard);
//
// Tenant-wide prevalence. SigninLogs only unless BaselineIncludeNonInteractive
// is true; the constant-false filter on the second leg stops it being read.
let IpBaseline = materialize(
    union isfuzzy=true
        (SigninLogs
        | where TimeGenerated between (BaselineStart .. FootprintEnd)
        | where IPAddress in (FootprintIpSet)
        | project TimeGenerated, IPAddress, UserId,
            Asn = iff(tostring(AutonomousSystemNumber) in ("", "0"), "", tostring(AutonomousSystemNumber)),
            Country = tostring(Location)),
        (AADNonInteractiveUserSignInLogs
        | where BaselineIncludeNonInteractive
        | where TimeGenerated between (BaselineStart .. FootprintEnd)
        | where IPAddress in (FootprintIpSet)
        | project TimeGenerated, IPAddress, UserId,
            Asn = iff(tostring(AutonomousSystemNumber) in ("", "0"), "", tostring(AutonomousSystemNumber)),
            Country = tostring(parse_json(tostring(LocationDetails)).countryOrRegion))
    | summarize
        BaselineUsers = dcount(UserId),
        BaselineDays = dcount(startofday(TimeGenerated)),
        BaselineFirstSeen = min(TimeGenerated),
        BaselineAsn = take_anyif(Asn, isnotempty(Asn)),
        BaselineCountry = take_anyif(Country, isnotempty(Country)),
        TargetFirstSeenOnIp = minif(TimeGenerated, UserId in (TargetIdSet))
        by IPAddress
);
//
// Classes, first match wins:
//   baseline incomplete  only seen in non-interactive logs, which the baseline skipped
//   no sign-in record    an audit IP with no sign-in from it anywhere in the baseline
//   campaign             CampaignMinUsers or more, all first seen inside NoveltyWindow
//   novel                fewer users than that, first seen inside NoveltyWindow
//   egress or VPN        EgressMinUsers or more across EgressMinDays or more
//   familiar             everything else
let Footprint = materialize(
    FootprintIps
    | lookup kind=leftouter IpBaseline on IPAddress
    | extend
        BaselineUsers = coalesce(BaselineUsers, tolong(0)),
        BaselineDays = coalesce(BaselineDays, tolong(0)),
        Asn = coalesce(FootprintAsn, BaselineAsn),
        Country = coalesce(FootprintCountry, BaselineCountry),
        TargetFirstOnIp = case(
            isnull(TargetFirstSeenOnIp), TargetFirstInFootprint,
            isnull(TargetFirstInFootprint), TargetFirstSeenOnIp,
            TargetFirstSeenOnIp < TargetFirstInFootprint, TargetFirstSeenOnIp,
            TargetFirstInFootprint)
    | extend AsnClass = case(
        isempty(Asn), "unknown",
        Asn in (HostingAsns), "hosting",
        Asn in (MicrosoftAsns), "Microsoft",
        "other")
    | extend FootprintClass = case(
        BaselineUsers == 0 and NonInteractiveHits > 0 and InteractiveHits == 0
            and not(BaselineIncludeNonInteractive), "baseline incomplete",
        BaselineUsers == 0, "no sign-in record",
        BaselineUsers >= CampaignMinUsers and BaselineFirstSeen >= NoveltyStart, "campaign",
        BaselineFirstSeen >= NoveltyStart, "novel",
        BaselineUsers >= EgressMinUsers and BaselineDays >= EgressMinDays, "egress or VPN",
        "familiar")
);
let FootprintDigest = toscalar(
    Footprint
    | extend Line = strcat(IPAddress, " ", FootprintClass, ", ", AsnClass,
        iff(isnotempty(Asn), strcat(" AS", Asn), ""), iff(isnotempty(Country), strcat(" ", Country), ""),
        ", users ", BaselineUsers, ", days ", BaselineDays)
    | summarize make_list(Line, 50)
);
// === SECTION 5: The Sessions ===
// How many times the door opened that day. The session count is distinct
// SessionIds with a successful sign-in for the target on the change day.
// CorrelationId is used only to stitch the steps of one sign-in (interrupt,
// MFA prompt, success) into a flow. It is never a session.
let SessionsByDay =
    UserSignins
    | where UserId in (TargetIdSet) or UserPrincipalName == TargetUpnLc
    | where ResultType == "0" and isnotempty(SessionId)
    | summarize SessionIdsOnDay = make_set(SessionId) by ChangeDay = startofday(TimeGenerated)
    | extend SessionCountOnDay = array_length(SessionIdsOnDay);
//
let FlowCorrelationIds = array_concat(
    toscalar(Spine | summarize make_set_if(OriginCorrelationId, isnotempty(OriginCorrelationId))),
    toscalar(Spine | summarize make_set_if(BridgeCorrelationId, isnotempty(BridgeCorrelationId))),
    EmptySetGuard);
let Flows = materialize(
    union isfuzzy=true
        (SigninLogs
        | where TimeGenerated between (SessionWalkStart .. FootprintEnd)
        | where UserId in (BridgedUserIds)
        | where CorrelationId in (FlowCorrelationIds)
        | project TimeGenerated, CorrelationId, ResultType = tostring(ResultType), SigninTable = "interactive"),
        (AADNonInteractiveUserSignInLogs
        | where TimeGenerated between (SessionWalkStart .. FootprintEnd)
        | where UserId in (BridgedUserIds)
        | where CorrelationId in (FlowCorrelationIds)
        | project TimeGenerated, CorrelationId, ResultType = tostring(ResultType), SigninTable = "non-interactive")
    | extend StepLabel = ResultLabel(ResultType)
    | extend Step = strcat(format_datetime(TimeGenerated, "yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss"), " ", ResultType,
        iff(isnotempty(StepLabel), strcat(" ", StepLabel), ""), " [", SigninTable, "]")
    | summarize Steps = make_list(Step, 30) by CorrelationId
    | extend Flow = strcat_array(array_sort_asc(Steps), " > ")
    | project CorrelationId, Flow
);
// === SECTION 6: The Premises ===
// Confirm the building is worth breaking into. Roles come from the latest
// IdentityInfo record per account. PIM activations by the target or the
// initiator within +/- PimWindow come from AuditLogs, matched on the
// initiator or any object ID inside TargetResources, because some activations
// are logged with a PIM service app as the initiator. The operation name
// shape ("... (PIM activation)") and the role sitting in
// TargetResources[0].displayName are unverified.
let Premises = materialize(
    union isfuzzy=true
        (datatable(TimeGenerated:datetime, AccountObjectId:string, AccountUPN:string, AssignedRoles:dynamic)[]),
        (IdentityInfo
        | where TimeGenerated between ((ScanEnd - IdentityInfoLookback) .. FootprintEnd)
        | where AccountObjectId in (UserIdSet) or AccountUPN in~ (UpnSet)
        | project TimeGenerated, AccountObjectId, AccountUPN, AssignedRoles)
    | extend AccountKey = coalesce(AccountObjectId, tolower(AccountUPN))
    | summarize arg_max(TimeGenerated, AssignedRoles) by AccountKey
    | extend PrivRolesHeld = set_intersect(AssignedRoles, PrivilegedRoles)
);
//
let PimEvents =
    AuditContext
    | where LoggedByService == "PIM" and OperationName has "PIM activation"
    | extend PimIds = set_union(pack_array(tostring(InitiatedBy.user.id)),
        extract_all(@'"id"\s*:\s*"([0-9a-fA-F-]{36})"', tostring(TargetResources)))
    | mv-expand PimUserId = PimIds to typeof(string)
    | where PimUserId in (UserIdSet)
    | distinct PimTime = TimeGenerated, PimUserId, PimRole = tostring(TargetResources[0].displayName);
let PimByChange =
    Changes
    | project ChangeId, EventTime, TargetId, Keys = set_union(pack_array(TargetId), pack_array(InitiatorId))
    | mv-expand UserKey = Keys to typeof(string)
    | where isnotempty(UserKey)
    | join kind=inner PimEvents on $left.UserKey == $right.PimUserId
    | where PimTime between ((EventTime - PimWindow) .. (EventTime + PimWindow))
    | summarize
        PimActivations = make_set(strcat(format_datetime(PimTime, "yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm"), " ", PimRole,
            iff(PimUserId == TargetId, " (target)", " (initiator)")), 20),
        PimTargetActivations = countif(PimUserId == TargetId)
        by ChangeId;
// === SECTION 7: After Hours ===
// What happened once the shop shut: activity inside PostChangeWindow by the
// target or the change's initiator.
let AfterHoursAudit =
    AuditContext
    | where Result =~ "success"
    | extend AhKind = case(
        OperationName has "member to role" and not(OperationName has "PIM activation"), "role assignment",
        OperationName in~ (AppConsentOps), "app consent",
        OperationName in~ (SpCredentialOps) or OperationName has "Certificates and secrets management", "SP credential",
        OperationName has "conditional access policy", "CA policy edit",
        "")
    | where isnotempty(AhKind)
    | extend AhUserId = tostring(InitiatedBy.user.id)
    | where AhUserId in (UserIdSet)
    | project AhTime = TimeGenerated, AhUserId, AhKind, AhOp = OperationName,
        AhTarget = tostring(TargetResources[0].displayName);
let AfterHoursByChange =
    Changes
    | project ChangeId, EventTime, Keys = set_union(pack_array(TargetId), pack_array(InitiatorId))
    | mv-expand UserKey = Keys to typeof(string)
    | where isnotempty(UserKey)
    | join kind=inner AfterHoursAudit on $left.UserKey == $right.AhUserId
    | where AhTime > EventTime and AhTime <= EventTime + PostChangeWindow
    | summarize
        AhRoleAssignments = countif(AhKind == "role assignment"),
        AhAppConsents = countif(AhKind == "app consent"),
        AhSpCredentials = countif(AhKind == "SP credential"),
        AhCaEdits = countif(AhKind == "CA policy edit"),
        AhActions = make_set(strcat(format_datetime(AhTime, "HH:mm"), " ", AhOp,
            iff(isnotempty(AhTarget), strcat(" (", AhTarget, ")"), "")), 20)
        by ChangeId;
//
// Inbox rules from OfficeActivity, optional table.
let InboxRules =
    union isfuzzy=true
        (datatable(TimeGenerated:datetime, UserId:string, Operation:string, ClientIP:string)[]),
        (OfficeActivity
        | where TimeGenerated between (ScanStart .. FootprintEnd)
        | where Operation in~ (InboxRuleOps)
        | where UserId in~ (UpnSet)
        | project TimeGenerated, UserId, Operation, ClientIP)
    | project IrTime = TimeGenerated, IrUpn = tolower(UserId), IrOp = Operation, IrIp = ClientIP;
let InboxByChange =
    Changes
    | project ChangeId, EventTime, Keys = set_union(pack_array(TargetUpnLower), pack_array(InitiatorUpn))
    | mv-expand UpnKey = Keys to typeof(string)
    | where isnotempty(UpnKey)
    | join kind=inner InboxRules on $left.UpnKey == $right.IrUpn
    | where IrTime > EventTime and IrTime <= EventTime + PostChangeWindow
    | summarize
        InboxRulesAfter = count(),
        InboxRuleActivity = make_set(strcat(format_datetime(IrTime, "HH:mm"), " ", IrOp, " from ", IrIp), 10)
        by ChangeId;
//
// The new method in use from new infrastructure: an interactive sign-in by
// the target, after an added or updated method, that succeeded with the same
// method family, from an IP that is novel, campaign, baseline incomplete,
// hosting, or first used by the target around the change.
let PostChangeMethodUse =
    UserSignins
    | where SigninTable == "interactive" and ResultType == "0"
    | where UserId in (TargetIdSet) or UserPrincipalName == TargetUpnLc
    | where TimeGenerated between (ScanStart .. FootprintEnd)
    | where AuthDetailsRaw has "succeeded"
    | project PsTime = TimeGenerated, PsIp = IPAddress, ad = parse_json(AuthDetailsRaw)
    | mv-expand ad
    | where tobool(ad.succeeded)
    | extend PsMethod = MethodFromText(tostring(ad.authenticationMethod))
    | where PsMethod !in ("Password", "Unknown")
    | distinct PsTime, PsIp, PsMethod
    | lookup kind=leftouter (
        Footprint
        | project PsIp = IPAddress, PsIpClass = FootprintClass, PsAsnClass = AsnClass, PsTargetFirstOnIp = TargetFirstOnIp
    ) on PsIp;
let NewMethodInfraByChange =
    Changes
    | where Action in ("added", "added and deleted", "updated")
    | project ChangeId, EventTime, MethodType, JoinKey = 1
    | join kind=inner (PostChangeMethodUse | extend JoinKey = 1) on JoinKey
    | where PsTime > EventTime and PsTime <= EventTime + PostChangeWindow
    | where MethodsMatch(MethodType, PsMethod)
    | where PsIpClass in ("novel", "campaign", "baseline incomplete") or PsAsnClass == "hosting"
        or (isnotnull(PsTargetFirstOnIp) and PsTargetFirstOnIp >= EventTime - PreChangeWindow)
    | summarize NewMethodInfraSignins = count(), NewMethodInfraIps = make_set(PsIp, 10) by ChangeId;
//
// Lockout pattern: a method added, then a method deleted on the same target
// within PostChangeWindow. Both rows of the pair carry the flag. A phone swap
// looks identical, which is why this is weight and never a hard flag.
let LockoutByChange =
    MethodChanges
    | where Action in ("added", "added and deleted")
    | project AddId = Id, AddTime = TimeGenerated, AddMethod = MethodType, AddTargetKey = TargetKey
    | join kind=inner (
        MethodChanges
        | where Action in ("deleted", "added and deleted")
        | project DelId = Id, DelTime = TimeGenerated, DelMethod = MethodType, DelTargetKey = TargetKey
    ) on $left.AddTargetKey == $right.DelTargetKey
    | where DelTime >= AddTime and DelTime <= AddTime + PostChangeWindow
    | extend Pair = strcat("added ", AddMethod, " at ", format_datetime(AddTime, "HH:mm"),
        ", deleted ", DelMethod, " at ", format_datetime(DelTime, "HH:mm"))
    | mv-expand ChangeId = pack_array(AddId, DelId) to typeof(string)
    | summarize LockoutDetail = make_set(Pair, 5) by ChangeId;
//
// Other accounts signing in from the change's audit IP around the change.
let NeighboursByChange =
    Changes
    | where isnotempty(InitiatorIp)
    | project ChangeId, EventTime, InitiatorIp, InitiatorId
    | join kind=inner (
        IpFallbackSignins
        | project NbTime = TimeGenerated, NbIp = IPAddress, NbUserId = UserId, NbUpn = UserPrincipalName
    ) on $left.InitiatorIp == $right.NbIp
    | where NbTime between ((EventTime - FallbackWindow) .. (EventTime + FallbackWindow))
    | where NbUserId != InitiatorId
    | summarize OtherAccountsOnChangeIp = make_set(NbUpn, 10), OtherAccountCount = dcount(NbUserId) by ChangeId;
// === SECTION 8: The Verdict ===
// One row per change. Weighted flags sum to Score; the two hard flags force
// Escalate while HardFlagsForceEscalate is true; the Narrative is one plain
// English sentence for the ticket.
Spine
| lookup kind=leftouter OriginMethods on ChangeId
| lookup kind=leftouter RegAfterChange on ChangeId
| lookup kind=leftouter RegisterCaByChange on ChangeId
| extend ChangeIp = coalesce(InitiatorIp, BridgeIp)
| lookup kind=leftouter (
    Footprint
    | project ChangeIp = IPAddress, ChangeIpClass = FootprintClass, ChangeIpAsn = Asn,
        ChangeIpAsnClass = AsnClass, ChangeIpCountry = Country, ChangeIpUsers = BaselineUsers,
        ChangeIpDays = BaselineDays, ChangeIpFirstSeen = BaselineFirstSeen
  ) on ChangeIp
| extend ChangeDay = startofday(EventTime)
| lookup kind=leftouter SessionsByDay on ChangeDay
| lookup kind=leftouter (Flows | project OriginCorrelationId = CorrelationId, OriginFlow = Flow) on OriginCorrelationId
| lookup kind=leftouter (Flows | project BridgeCorrelationId = CorrelationId, BridgeFlow = Flow) on BridgeCorrelationId
| extend
    TargetPremisesKey = coalesce(TargetId, TargetUpnLower),
    InitiatorPremisesKey = coalesce(InitiatorId, InitiatorUpn)
| lookup kind=leftouter (
    Premises | project TargetPremisesKey = AccountKey, TargetRoles = AssignedRoles, TargetPrivRoles = PrivRolesHeld
  ) on TargetPremisesKey
| lookup kind=leftouter (
    Premises | project InitiatorPremisesKey = AccountKey, InitiatorPrivRoles = PrivRolesHeld
  ) on InitiatorPremisesKey
| lookup kind=leftouter PimByChange on ChangeId
| lookup kind=leftouter AfterHoursByChange on ChangeId
| lookup kind=leftouter InboxByChange on ChangeId
| lookup kind=leftouter NewMethodInfraByChange on ChangeId
| lookup kind=leftouter LockoutByChange on ChangeId
| lookup kind=leftouter NeighboursByChange on ChangeId
//
// --- Fill the gaps left by unmatched lookups ---
| extend
    BridgeMethod = coalesce(BridgeMethod, "none"),
    PimTargetActivations = coalesce(PimTargetActivations, tolong(0)),
    AhRoleAssignments = coalesce(AhRoleAssignments, tolong(0)),
    AhAppConsents = coalesce(AhAppConsents, tolong(0)),
    AhSpCredentials = coalesce(AhSpCredentials, tolong(0)),
    AhCaEdits = coalesce(AhCaEdits, tolong(0)),
    InboxRulesAfter = coalesce(InboxRulesAfter, tolong(0)),
    NewMethodInfraSignins = coalesce(NewMethodInfraSignins, tolong(0)),
    OtherAccountCount = coalesce(OtherAccountCount, tolong(0)),
    SessionCountOnDay = coalesce(SessionCountOnDay, tolong(0))
//
// --- Strength, device, privilege and path features ---
| extend
    OriginTokenClaimSeen = OriginAuthDetailsRaw contains TokenClaimText,
    BridgeTokenClaimSeen = BridgeAuthDetailsRaw contains TokenClaimText,
    OriginPossiblyTruncated = UseWalk and OriginTime <= SessionWalkStart + OriginBoundaryTolerance,
    OriginDevice = parse_json(OriginDeviceRaw),
    ChangeDevice = parse_json(iff(isnotnull(BridgeTime), BridgeDeviceRaw, OriginDeviceRaw)),
    OriginMfaMethods = set_difference(OriginMethodsUsed, dynamic(["Password", "Previously satisfied"])),
    OriginAsnClass = case(
        isempty(OriginAsn), "unknown",
        OriginAsn in (HostingAsns), "hosting",
        OriginAsn in (MicrosoftAsns), "Microsoft",
        "other"),
    RegisterCaApplied = coalesce(array_length(RegisterCaPolicies), 0) > 0,
    TargetIsPrivileged = coalesce(array_length(TargetPrivRoles), 0) > 0 or PimTargetActivations > 0,
    ChangePathClass = case(
        isempty(BridgeAppId) and IsAppMadeChange, "app-made change",
        isempty(BridgeAppId), "no sign-in bridged",
        BridgeAppId == MySigninsAppId or BridgeAppId in (AdditionalExpectedAppIds), "expected (My Signins)",
        BridgeAppId in (WindowsSignInAppIds), "WHfB provisioning (Windows Sign In)",
        BridgeAppId in (ScriptedAppIds) or BridgeAppName contains "PowerShell" or BridgeAppName contains "Command Line",
            "scripted (Graph or PowerShell)",
        "unfamiliar app")
| extend
    OriginDeviceTrust = tostring(OriginDevice.trustType),
    OriginDeviceCompliant = tostring(OriginDevice.isCompliant),
    OriginDeviceRegistered = isnotempty(tostring(OriginDevice.deviceId)) or isnotempty(tostring(OriginDevice.trustType)),
    ChangeDeviceTrust = tostring(ChangeDevice.trustType),
    ChangeDeviceCompliant = tostring(ChangeDevice.isCompliant),
    ChangeDeviceOs = tostring(ChangeDevice.operatingSystem),
    ChangeDeviceRegistered = isnotempty(tostring(ChangeDevice.deviceId)) or isnotempty(tostring(ChangeDevice.trustType))
//
// --- Flags ---
| extend
    OriginMfaPerformed = coalesce(array_length(OriginMfaMethods), 0) > 0,
    OriginIsWalkedFirst = UseWalk and not(OriginPossiblyTruncated)
| extend
    F_TokenClaimAtOrigin = OriginIsWalkedFirst and OriginTokenClaimSeen and not(OriginMfaPerformed)
        and (not(TokenClaimIgnoreRegisteredDevice) or not(OriginDeviceRegistered)),
    F_SingleFactorThenReg = OriginIsWalkedFirst and OriginTable == "interactive"
        and OriginAuthRequirement == "singleFactorAuthentication"
        and not(OriginMfaPerformed) and not(OriginTokenClaimSeen)
        and isnotnull(RegistrationCompletedAt),
    F_CampaignIp = ChangeIpClass == "campaign",
    F_LockoutPattern = coalesce(array_length(LockoutDetail), 0) > 0,
    F_PrivilegedActionAfter = AhRoleAssignments + AhAppConsents + AhSpCredentials + AhCaEdits > 0,
    F_NovelIp = ChangeIpClass == "novel",
    F_HostingAsn = ChangeIpAsnClass == "hosting" or OriginAsnClass == "hosting",
    F_PhoneDowngrade = TargetIsPrivileged and MethodType startswith "Phone"
        and Action in ("added", "default changed", "updated", "added and deleted"),
    F_ScriptedChangePath = ChangePathClass startswith "scripted",
    F_UnfamiliarChangePath = ChangePathClass == "unfamiliar app",
    F_NewMethodFromNewInfra = NewMethodInfraSignins > 0,
    F_InboxRuleAfter = InboxRulesAfter > 0,
    F_RiskySignin = OriginRisk in ("medium", "high") or BridgeRisk in ("medium", "high"),
    F_SessionAsnHop = UseWalk and isnotempty(OriginAsn) and isnotempty(BridgeAsn) and OriginAsn != BridgeAsn,
    F_TapIssued = IsTapIssued,
    F_AppMadeChange = IsAppMadeChange,
    F_UnmanagedDevice = isnotnull(BridgeTime) and not(ChangeDeviceRegistered) and ChangeDeviceCompliant != "true",
    F_NoSigninBridged = BridgeMethod == "none" and not(IsAppMadeChange),
    F_ChangeIpUnseen = ChangeIpClass == "no sign-in record",
    F_FallbackBridge = BridgeMethod startswith "fallback",
    F_BaselineIncomplete = ChangeIpClass == "baseline incomplete",
    F_NoRegisterCaPolicy = isnotnull(BridgeTime) and not(RegisterCaApplied)
| extend F_MicrosoftAsn = not(F_HostingAsn) and (ChangeIpAsnClass == "Microsoft" or OriginAsnClass == "Microsoft")
| extend Score =
      iff(F_TokenClaimAtOrigin, W_TokenClaimAtOrigin, 0)
    + iff(F_SingleFactorThenReg, W_SingleFactorThenReg, 0)
    + iff(F_CampaignIp, W_CampaignIp, 0)
    + iff(F_LockoutPattern, W_LockoutPattern, 0)
    + iff(F_PrivilegedActionAfter, W_PrivilegedActionAfter, 0)
    + iff(F_NovelIp, W_NovelIp, 0)
    + iff(F_HostingAsn, W_HostingAsn, 0)
    + iff(F_PhoneDowngrade, W_PhoneDowngrade, 0)
    + iff(F_ScriptedChangePath, W_ScriptedChangePath, 0)
    + iff(F_UnfamiliarChangePath, W_UnfamiliarChangePath, 0)
    + iff(F_NewMethodFromNewInfra, W_NewMethodFromNewInfra, 0)
    + iff(F_InboxRuleAfter, W_InboxRuleAfter, 0)
    + iff(F_RiskySignin, W_RiskySignin, 0)
    + iff(F_SessionAsnHop, W_SessionAsnHop, 0)
    + iff(F_TapIssued, W_TapIssued, 0)
    + iff(F_AppMadeChange, W_AppMadeChange, 0)
    + iff(F_MicrosoftAsn, W_MicrosoftAsn, 0)
    + iff(F_UnmanagedDevice, W_UnmanagedDevice, 0)
    + iff(F_NoSigninBridged, W_NoSigninBridged, 0)
    + iff(F_ChangeIpUnseen, W_ChangeIpUnseen, 0)
    + iff(F_FallbackBridge, W_FallbackBridge, 0)
    + iff(F_BaselineIncomplete, W_BaselineIncomplete, 0)
    + iff(F_NoRegisterCaPolicy, W_NoRegisterCaPolicy, 0)
| extend Flags = array_concat(
    iff(F_TokenClaimAtOrigin,    pack_array(strcat("token-claim MFA at session origin +", W_TokenClaimAtOrigin)), dynamic([])),
    iff(F_SingleFactorThenReg,   pack_array(strcat("single-factor sign-in then full registration +", W_SingleFactorThenReg)), dynamic([])),
    iff(F_CampaignIp,            pack_array(strcat("campaign IP +", W_CampaignIp)), dynamic([])),
    iff(F_LockoutPattern,        pack_array(strcat("lockout pattern (added then deleted) +", W_LockoutPattern)), dynamic([])),
    iff(F_PrivilegedActionAfter, pack_array(strcat("privileged action afterwards +", W_PrivilegedActionAfter)), dynamic([])),
    iff(F_NovelIp,               pack_array(strcat("novel IP +", W_NovelIp)), dynamic([])),
    iff(F_HostingAsn,            pack_array(strcat("hosting ASN +", W_HostingAsn)), dynamic([])),
    iff(F_PhoneDowngrade,        pack_array(strcat("phone or SMS on a privileged account +", W_PhoneDowngrade)), dynamic([])),
    iff(F_ScriptedChangePath,    pack_array(strcat("scripted change path +", W_ScriptedChangePath)), dynamic([])),
    iff(F_UnfamiliarChangePath,  pack_array(strcat("unfamiliar change path +", W_UnfamiliarChangePath)), dynamic([])),
    iff(F_NewMethodFromNewInfra, pack_array(strcat("new method used from new infrastructure +", W_NewMethodFromNewInfra)), dynamic([])),
    iff(F_InboxRuleAfter,        pack_array(strcat("inbox rule afterwards +", W_InboxRuleAfter)), dynamic([])),
    iff(F_RiskySignin,           pack_array(strcat("risky sign-in +", W_RiskySignin)), dynamic([])),
    iff(F_SessionAsnHop,         pack_array(strcat("session changed ASN since origin +", W_SessionAsnHop)), dynamic([])),
    iff(F_TapIssued,             pack_array(strcat("Temporary Access Pass issued +", W_TapIssued)), dynamic([])),
    iff(F_AppMadeChange,         pack_array(strcat("change made by an app +", W_AppMadeChange)), dynamic([])),
    iff(F_MicrosoftAsn,          pack_array(strcat("Microsoft ASN +", W_MicrosoftAsn)), dynamic([])),
    iff(F_UnmanagedDevice,       pack_array(strcat("unregistered, non-compliant device +", W_UnmanagedDevice)), dynamic([])),
    iff(F_NoSigninBridged,       pack_array(strcat("no sign-in bridged +", W_NoSigninBridged)), dynamic([])),
    iff(F_ChangeIpUnseen,        pack_array(strcat("change IP never signed in +", W_ChangeIpUnseen)), dynamic([])),
    iff(F_FallbackBridge,        pack_array(strcat("fallback bridge +", W_FallbackBridge)), dynamic([])),
    iff(F_BaselineIncomplete,    pack_array(strcat("baseline incomplete +", W_BaselineIncomplete)), dynamic([])),
    iff(F_NoRegisterCaPolicy,    pack_array(strcat("no register-security-info CA policy applied +", W_NoRegisterCaPolicy)), dynamic([])))
| extend FlagCount = array_length(Flags)
| extend Verdict = case(
    HardFlagsForceEscalate and (F_TokenClaimAtOrigin or F_SingleFactorThenReg), "Escalate",
    Score >= EscalateThreshold, "Escalate",
    Score >= ReviewThreshold, "Review",
    "Benign")
| extend LeadFlag = case(
    F_TokenClaimAtOrigin, "token-claim MFA at session origin",
    F_SingleFactorThenReg, "a single-factor sign-in followed by full registration",
    F_CampaignIp, "a campaign IP",
    F_LockoutPattern, "a lockout pattern",
    F_PrivilegedActionAfter, "privileged activity afterwards",
    F_NovelIp, "a novel IP",
    F_HostingAsn, "a hosting ASN",
    F_PhoneDowngrade, "phone or SMS on a privileged account",
    F_ScriptedChangePath, "a scripted change path",
    F_UnfamiliarChangePath, "an unfamiliar change path",
    F_NewMethodFromNewInfra, "the new method used from new infrastructure",
    F_InboxRuleAfter, "an inbox rule afterwards",
    F_RiskySignin, "a risky sign-in",
    F_SessionAsnHop, "an ASN change inside the session",
    F_TapIssued, "a Temporary Access Pass",
    F_AppMadeChange, "an app making the change",
    "minor signals")
//
// --- Narrative: one sentence, assembled from parts ---
| extend
    _who = case(
        ChangeKind == "self-service", TargetUpnLower,
        ChangeKind == "admin", strcat("Admin ", InitiatorUpn),
        ChangeKind == "app", strcat("The app ", coalesce(InitiatorAppName, InitiatorAppId, "(unnamed)")),
        "An unknown initiator"),
    _method = iff(MethodType == "Unknown", "an authentication method", MethodType),
    _onWhom = iff(ChangeKind == "self-service", " on their own account", strcat(" on ", TargetUpnLower)),
    _when = strcat(" at ", format_datetime(EventTime, "yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm"), " UTC"),
    _origin = format_datetime(OriginTime, "yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm")
| extend
    _what = case(
        Action == "added", strcat(" added ", _method),
        Action == "deleted", strcat(" deleted ", _method),
        Action == "default changed", strcat(" changed the default method (", _method, ")"),
        Action == "added and deleted", strcat(" added and deleted ", _method),
        strcat(" updated ", _method)),
    _path = case(
        BridgeMethod startswith "initiator", strcat(" via ", coalesce(BridgeAppName, BridgeAppId, "an unnamed app"),
            iff(BridgeMethod has "did not match", " (sign-in IP differs from the audit IP)", "")),
        BridgeMethod startswith "fallback", strcat(" with no sign-in inside the pre-change window, so it was bridged on IP and a +/-",
            FallbackMinutes, " minute window only (", coalesce(BridgeAppName, "unnamed app"), ")"),
        ChangeKind == "app", " with no user session behind it",
        OtherAccountCount > 0, strcat(" with no initiator sign-in to bridge, even on IP and a +/-", FallbackMinutes,
            " minute window, though ", OtherAccountCount, " other account(s) signed in from that IP"),
        strcat(" with no initiator sign-in to bridge, even on IP and a +/-", FallbackMinutes, " minute window")),
    _ip = iff(isempty(ChangeIp), "", strcat(" from ", ChangeIp, " (", coalesce(ChangeIpClass, "unclassified"),
        iff(isnotempty(ChangeIpAsn), strcat(", AS", ChangeIpAsn, " ", ChangeIpAsnClass), ""),
        iff(isnotempty(ChangeIpCountry), strcat(", ", ChangeIpCountry), ""), ")")),
    _auth = case(
        OriginMfaPerformed, strcat("with MFA (", strcat_array(OriginMfaMethods, ", "), ")"),
        OriginTokenClaimSeen, strcat("on a token-claim MFA", iff(OriginDeviceRegistered, " from a registered device", "")),
        OriginAuthRequirement == "singleFactorAuthentication", "on single-factor authentication",
        strcat("with ", coalesce(OriginAuthRequirement, "unrecorded authentication"))),
    _originTable = iff(OriginTable == "non-interactive", " (a non-interactive record)", "")
| extend
    _session = case(
        OriginSource == "none", "",
        F_TokenClaimAtOrigin, strcat(", in a session that first appeared at ", _origin,
            " on a token-claim MFA with no MFA step of its own"),
        F_SingleFactorThenReg, strcat(", in a session that began at ", _origin,
            " on single-factor authentication and went on to complete registration"),
        not(UseWalk), strcat(", on a sign-in at ", _origin, " with no session to walk, ", _auth),
        OriginPossiblyTruncated, strcat(", in a session older than the walk, first seen at ", _origin, _originTable, " ", _auth),
        strcat(", in a session that began at ", _origin, _originTable, " ", _auth)),
    _close = iff(FlagCount == 0,
        strcat("; no flags fired, so ", Verdict, "."),
        strcat("; lead signal ", LeadFlag, ", ", FlagCount, iff(FlagCount == 1, " flag", " flags"),
            ", score ", Score, ", so ", Verdict, "."))
| extend Narrative = strcat(_who, _what, _onWhom, _when, _path, _ip, _session, _close)
| extend
    TargetPrivilege = case(
        coalesce(array_length(TargetPrivRoles), 0) > 0, strcat_array(TargetPrivRoles, ", "),
        PimTargetActivations > 0, "PIM activation seen near the change",
        isnull(TargetRoles), "unknown (no IdentityInfo record)",
        "no privileged role found"),
    InitiatorPrivilege = case(
        ChangeKind != "admin", "",
        coalesce(array_length(InitiatorPrivRoles), 0) > 0, strcat_array(InitiatorPrivRoles, ", "),
        "no privileged role found"),
    Initiator = case(
        ChangeKind == "app", strcat("[app] ", coalesce(InitiatorAppName, InitiatorAppId)),
        coalesce(InitiatorUpn, InitiatorId))
| project
    Verdict, Score, Narrative, Flags,
    EventTime, OperationName, Action, MethodType, ChangeKind, MethodDetail,
    Target = TargetUpnLower, TargetPrivilege, Initiator, InitiatorId, InitiatorPrivilege, InitiatorIp, InitiatorAppId,
    ChangeIp, ChangeIpClass, ChangeIpAsn, ChangeIpAsnClass, ChangeIpCountry, ChangeIpUsers, ChangeIpDays,
    ChangeIpFirstSeen, OtherAccountsOnChangeIp,
    BridgeMethod, ChangePathClass, BridgeTime, BridgeTable, BridgeAppName, BridgeAppId, BridgeIp,
    BridgeSessionId, BridgeTokenClaimSeen, BridgeFlow,
    OriginSource, OriginTime, OriginPossiblyTruncated, OriginTable, OriginAppName, OriginIp, OriginAsn,
    OriginAsnClass, OriginCountry, OriginAuthRequirement, OriginMfaMethods, OriginTokenClaimSeen,
    OriginRisk, OriginDeviceTrust, OriginDeviceCompliant, OriginUserAgent, OriginFlow,
    ChangeDeviceTrust, ChangeDeviceCompliant, ChangeDeviceOs,
    RegisterCaApplied, RegisterCaPolicies, RegistrationCompletedAt,
    SessionCountOnDay, SessionIdsOnDay, PimActivations,
    AfterHoursActions = AhActions, InboxRuleActivity, NewMethodInfraIps, LockoutDetail, IsTapIssued,
    ModifiedProps, EchoesSuppressed = EchoCount, UserFootprint = FootprintDigest, ChangeId, AuditCorrelationId
| sort by EventTime asc
// | lookup kind=leftouter CorrelationBridge on ChangeId    // CORRELATION TEST: see SECTION 2
